Evaluation memo: keep memoized nodes alive for the whole scope (AlteredBGA, apply with `patch -p1`)

AbstractNode::memoized keys its results on spl_object_id($this). ActivateCard::getFlowTree builds a
new tree every time it is asked something (isOptional, isDoable...), and that tree is freed right
after. PHP gives a freed object's id to the next object created, so the next flow tree built in the
same Evaluation scope gets the same key and the previous tree's cached answers. Without the memo
(the engine before Evaluation.php, and the Rust translation) this does not happen.

Reproduce: whole-game golden seed 21 (`explore.php game 21 --dump=36`), step 36: EndOfNight PARALLEL
of player 2002 with Armored Jammer (LeaveLandmark: Target upTo, optional) and Aerolith Reef
(Discard/isSacrificed: Resupply, mandatory). Inside one scope the Aerolith child's isOptional returns
true (the cached answer of a freed tree), so getChoices adds Pass (99); outside a scope it returns
false and there is no Pass. With this patch the PHP decision matches the unmemoized engine and the
Rust translation (checked by loading the step-36 tables into a patched copy of the game,
GAME_DIR=/tmp/gamefix in the container).

Fix: Evaluation::run takes the object to pin; pinned objects are released when the outermost scope ends.

diff -ru a/modules/php/Core/Engine/AbstractNode.php b/modules/php/Core/Engine/AbstractNode.php
--- a/modules/php/Core/Engine/AbstractNode.php	2026-10-29 11:20:36
+++ b/modules/php/Core/Engine/AbstractNode.php	2026-10-29 11:20:47
@@ -417,7 +417,9 @@
    */
   protected function memoized(string $what, $player, callable $compute)
   {
-    return Evaluation::run('node|' . spl_object_id($this) . '|' . $what . '|' . (is_null($player) ? '' : $player->getId()), $compute);
+    // $this is pinned: a node built for one question (ActivateCard::getFlowTree) is freed right
+    // after, and the next node built would otherwise reuse its id and get its results
+    return Evaluation::run('node|' . spl_object_id($this) . '|' . $what . '|' . (is_null($player) ? '' : $player->getId()), $compute, $this);
   }
 
   public function isAutomatic($player = null)
diff -ru a/modules/php/Helpers/Evaluation.php b/modules/php/Helpers/Evaluation.php
--- a/modules/php/Helpers/Evaluation.php	2026-10-29 11:20:36
+++ b/modules/php/Helpers/Evaluation.php	2026-10-29 11:20:44
@@ -12,14 +12,20 @@
 class Evaluation
 {
   protected static ?array $results = null;
+  /** Objects whose spl_object_id is part of a key: kept alive until the scope ends, so that no
+   *  other object gets the same id (and the same cached results) within the scope */
+  protected static array $pinned = [];
 
   /** Runs $compute once per key within the scope, opening the scope if none is open */
-  public static function run(string $key, callable $compute)
+  public static function run(string $key, callable $compute, ?object $pin = null)
   {
     $outermost = self::$results === null;
     if ($outermost) {
       self::$results = [];
     }
+    if ($pin !== null) {
+      self::$pinned[spl_object_id($pin)] = $pin;
+    }
     try {
       if (!array_key_exists($key, self::$results)) {
         self::$results[$key] = $compute();
@@ -28,6 +34,7 @@
     } finally {
       if ($outermost) {
         self::$results = null;
+        self::$pinned = [];
       }
     }
   }
